## 8. Tests

- `tests/unit/test_health.py` — root + health endpoint tests
- `tests/conftest.py` — async HTTP client fixture

Run: `pytest -v`

---

## 9. Environment Variables

See `.env.example`. Minimum required:
- `SECRET_KEY`, `JWT_SECRET_KEY`
- `DATABASE_URL`, `DATABASE_SYNC_URL`
- `REDIS_URL`

---

## 10. How To Run

```bash
# 1. Configure
cp .env.example .env

# 2. Start stack
docker compose up -d --build

# 3. Migrate
docker compose exec backend alembic upgrade head

# 4. Verify
curl http://localhost:8000/api/v1/health
curl http://localhost:8000/api/v1/health/db
curl http://localhost:8000/api/v1/health/redis



### 4.32 CI env note

The `tests.yml` workflow uses **SQLite for tests** (the conftest override). MySQL/Redis services are declared so integration tests that want them can use them — the current suite doesn't require them.

---

## 5. Files Modified

| File | Change |
|---|---|
| `backend/app/main.py` | Sentry init, Gzip, `/health/live` + `/health/ready`, hide docs in prod, mount static |
| `backend/app/web/views.py` | Inject `env` + `sentry_dsn` into all template contexts |
| `backend/app/api/v1/__init__.py` | Register `notes`, `users` |
| `backend/app/api/v1/courses.py` | Add `GET /teacher/courses/{id}/students` |
| `backend/app/schemas/__init__.py` | Export note schemas |
| `frontend/templates/base.html` | Load `monitoring.js` + env/DSN globals |
| `docker-compose.yml` | + nginx + certbot + backups volume |
| `README.md` | Final rewrite |

